.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resume PDF
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recommended: KEEP resume/Resume.pdf committed in a PRIVATE repo so that
# GitHub Actions can find it when it checks out the code.
#
# If the repository is PUBLIC, you should NOT expose your resume.
# Uncomment the line below to ignore it — but remember the scheduled
# workflow will then fail (no file to upload). Use a private repo instead,
# or attach the resume in a way you control (see README).
# resume/Resume.pdf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor cruft
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
